    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-29T21:25:37+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-29T21:25:37+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-29T10:55:37Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-29T10:55:37Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A ridge of high pressure lies over eastern parts of SA, while a low pressure system in WA extends a trough into the west. The low and trough will move across the state on Friday, clearing to the east by Saturday morning as a brief high pressure system settles over SA. Another low is expected to enter from the west on Sunday, moving over central and eastern parts on Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW005" description="Lower South East" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-29T21:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-30T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-29T10:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-29T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Clear. Light winds.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-30T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-31T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-29T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-30T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny morning. High chance of showers in the evening. The chance of a thunderstorm at night. Light winds becoming northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the morning then tending northerly 20 to 30 km/h in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to around 9 with daytime temperatures reaching the high 20s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">No Rating</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 4:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-31T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-30T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm in the early morning. Winds northerly 20 to 30 km/h turning westerly 25 to 40 km/h early in the morning then decreasing to 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 14 with daytime temperatures reaching around 20.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-02T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-01T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the morning. Winds westerly 15 to 20 km/h tending southwesterly during the afternoon then becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-02T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-03T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-01T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-02T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h turning southerly 15 to 25 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
